-- title:
--   Pairing cochain χsmileκₐ differs from inflated carry by a level coboundary
-- statement:
--   Let $K\subseteq\Omega$ be fields with $\Omega$ a Galois $K$-algebra, let $p$ be prime, and let $r$ be a group homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/K)$ to $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ which is assumed cofinal for levels in the sense of `hlevel`: for every intermediate field $E$ of $\Omega/K$ finite over $K$ there is an intermediate field $F$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}$ such that every $\sigma$ with $r\sigma$ in the fixing subgroup of $F$ lies in the fixing subgroup of $E$. Let $\chi\colon\mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/K)\to\mathbb{Z}$ satisfy the predicate `IsLevelConstant₁ r χ` and $p\mid\chi\sigma+\chi\tau-\chi(\sigma\tau)$ for all $\sigma,\tau$. Let $K_\chi$ be an intermediate field, finite-dimensional and normal over $K$, whose fixing subgroup consists exactly of the $\sigma$ with $p\mid\chi\sigma$, and let $s\in\mathrm{Gal}(K_\chi/K)$ be of finite order with every element of that group a power of $s$, such that $p\mid\chi\sigma-\log_s(\sigma|_{K_\chi})$, where $\log_s$ denotes `cyclicLog`, the index in $\mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{ord}\,s)$ attached to an element by the enumeration of the cyclic group generated by $s$. Finally let $a\in K^\times$ and $\alpha\in\Omega^\times$ with $a=\alpha^{p}$ in $\Omega$. The assertion is that the $2$-cochain sending $(\sigma,\tau)$ to the image in $\Omega^\times$ (written additively, via the ℤ-linear map induced by the inclusion of the $p$-th roots of unity) of $\chi(\sigma)\cdot\sigma\bigl(\tau\alpha/\alpha\bigr)$, minus the value at $(\sigma,\tau)$ of `unitsInflate₂ Kχ` applied to `carryFun s hs hfin` of the image of $a$ in $K_\chi^\times$ — that is, of the cochain equal to $a$ when $\log_s(\sigma|_{K_\chi})+\log_s(\tau|_{K_\chi})\ge\mathrm{ord}\,s$ and $0$ otherwise — belongs to `levelCoboundaries₂ r (Rep.ofAlgebraAutOnUnits K Ω)`.
--
--   This is the cochain-level form of the classical identity identifying the cup product of a character $\chi$ with a Kummer class $\kappa_a$ with the inflation of the cyclic-algebra (carry) cocycle of $a$, as in the treatment of cyclic algebras and local invariants in Serre's Corps Locaux, Ch. XIV. It feeds the computation of local invariants of such classes and the criterion for a cup product class to be a level coboundary, being used by [`groupCohomology.exists_levelCocycles2_ofChar_cycloChar_isLocalInv_witness`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_levelCocycles2_ofChar_cycloChar_isLocalInv_witness), [`groupCohomology.localInv_smul_kummerCocycle_eq_apply_frobenius_mul_valuation`](thm.html#groupCohomology.localInv_smul_kummerCocycle_eq_apply_frobenius_mul_valuation) and [`groupCohomology.smul_kummerCocycle_mem_levelCoboundaries2_iff_exists_norm_eq`](thm.html#groupCohomology.smul_kummerCocycle_mem_levelCoboundaries2_iff_exists_norm_eq).
